        "original_id": "689c8afd-5587-5d65-b5d9-ef9c211b0a5c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: The Simpsons Theme\n- People: Danny Elfman, Matt Groening, Alf Clausen\n- Roles: series creator, composer, scorer, orchestrator\n- Topics: television music, opening sequences\n\nFacts:\n- In 1989, Danny Elfman composed The Simpsons Theme after series creator Matt Groening approached him and requested a retro-style theme.\n- The Simpsons Theme plays during the opening sequence of The Simpsons.\n- Alf Clausen has scored or orchestrated music for more than 30 films and television shows.\n- Alf Clausen's scoring or orchestration credits include Moonlighting, The Naked Gun, ALF, and Ferris Bueller's Day Off.",
